---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="ShotMark Privacy" description="How ShotMark handles your screenshots, on-device text recognition, optional iCloud sync, and website privacy." canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <main id="main-content" class="document-page wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Your screenshots.<br />Your space.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Your library stays on your device by default. Optional iCloud sync uses your Apple account. No separate ShotMark account required.</p>
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-19">19 October 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="storage-title">
        <h2 id="storage-title">What the app stores</h2>
        <p>ShotMark stores the screenshots you add and the context you create, including titles, notes, Collections, Projects, tags, detected text, voice notes, reminders, and app settings. This information makes up your library and is stored for your use.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="permissions-title">
        <h2 id="permissions-title">Access you choose</h2>
        <p>Photo access lets you choose screenshots to add. On Mac, imports and folder watching use files or folders you select. Microphone access is used when you record a voice note, and notification permission supports reminders. You can manage these permissions in your device’s settings.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="recognition-title">
        <h2 id="recognition-title">Text recognition and exports</h2>
        <p>ShotMark uses Apple Vision to recognize text on your device. Screenshots do not need to be sent to a third-party text-recognition service for this process. Detected text is saved with the card so you can view, copy, or search it when the relevant feature is available.</p>
        <p>When you export or share a card, you choose where it goes. The destination app or service has its own privacy practices.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="icloud-title">
        <h2 id="icloud-title">Optional iCloud sync</h2>
        <p>If you enable iCloud sync, ShotMark uses your Apple account and Apple’s iCloud services to make your library available across your devices. This is optional; you can use ShotMark with a local library.</p>
        <p>Apple’s handling of its services is described in <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="tracking-title">
        <h2 id="tracking-title">No ads or third-party tracking in the app</h2>
        <p>ShotMark does not include third-party advertising or tracking SDKs. The developer does not collect your screenshot library from the app.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="website-title">
        <h2 id="website-title">This website</h2>
        <p>This website does not add analytics scripts, advertising trackers, or analytics or advertising cookies. Its hosting provider may process ordinary web request information, such as IP addresses and requested pages, to deliver and protect the site.</p>
        <p>App Store links take you to Apple’s website. Email links open your email app. Those services follow their own privacy practices.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title">Questions and support</h2>
        <p>If you email support, the message and any attachments you choose to send are used to respond to your request. Please avoid including sensitive information that is not needed to explain the issue.</p>
        <p>For privacy questions, contact <a href="mailto:hello@zhenchyi.com?subject=ShotMark%20Privacy">hello@zhenchyi.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
